B.eE1=new A.eo("microwave","Microwave","\ud83c\udf72",B.cS,"The plate turns and the timer counts down. Needs a lot of power: 8 to 13.5 volts. Works either way round.","A tube makes invisible microwaves that shake the water in food so it gets hot.")
B.eEK=new A.eo("doorbell","Doorbell","\ud83d\udd14",B.bt,"Swings its bell and goes ding-dong. Needs 3 to 12 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A little hammer, pulled by a magnet, hits a metal bar again and again.")
B.eEe=new A.eo("camera","Security camera","\ud83d\udcf7",B.an,"A red REC light blinks and the lens looks around. Needs 4 to 12 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A small sensor turns light into numbers, many times a second, and a chip makes them into a video.")
B.eEE=new A.eo("console","Game console","\ud83c\udfae",B.bk,"Plays a little ball game on its screen. Needs 4.5 to 9.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A fast chip draws the picture over and over, many times each second.")
B.eEV=new A.eo("heartmon","Heart monitor","\ud83e\ude7a",B.hF,"Draws a heartbeat line and beeps. Needs 3 to 9 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","Sensors on the body feel tiny electric signals made by the heart and a chip draws them as a line.")
B.eE_=new A.eo("aquarium","Aquarium","\ud83d\udc20",B.bc,"A pump blows bubbles and a fish swims around. Needs 3 to 9 volts. Works either way round.","A small motor pushes air through a stone, making lots of tiny bubbles.")
B.eEz=new A.eo("lighthouse","Lighthouse","\ud83d\uddfc",B.eD,"A bright beam sweeps round and round. Needs 4 to 13.5 volts. Works either way round.","A huge lamp sits inside a glass lens that squeezes the light into a beam. A motor turns the lens.")
B.eEH=new A.eo("discoball","Disco ball","\ud83e\udea9",B.oF,"Spins and throws sparkles everywhere. Needs 5 to 13.5 volts. Works either way round.","Hundreds of tiny mirrors on a ball bounce a spotlight all around the room as it turns.")
B.eF_=new A.eo("robot","Robot","\ud83e\udd16",B.aH,"Its eyes light up and blink, and its arm waves. Needs 4 to 9 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A tiny computer reads sensors and tells small motors in the arms and head what to do.")
B.eDY=new A.eo("toaster","Toaster","\ud83c\udf5e",B.ed,"Glowing wires toast the bread, then it pops up. Needs 3.5 to 13 volts and a strong battery. Works either way round.","Thin wires get red hot as the current squeezes through them and toast the bread.")
